# The Machine-Generated Code Disclaimer and Release

**(MGCDR) Version 1.0**

---

## PREAMBLE AND RECITALS

**WHEREAS**, the source code, object code, scripts, configuration files, and associated documentation accompanying this instrument (collectively, the "**Software**") were generated, in whole or in substantial part, by one or more large language models or other generative artificial intelligence systems (each, a "**Generative Model**") in response to natural-language prompts, a practice colloquially referred to as "vibe coding";

**WHEREAS**, the person or entity distributing the Software (the "**Distributor**") did not exercise sufficient creative control over the expressive elements of the Software to constitute traditional human authorship thereof;

**WHEREAS**, in the United States, the courts and the United States Copyright Office have held that copyright protection subsists only in works of human authorship, and that material generated by an artificial intelligence system without sufficient human creative contribution is not eligible for copyright protection (*see, e.g.*, *Thaler v. Perlmutter*, 687 F. Supp. 3d 140 (D.D.C. 2023), *aff'd*, No. 23-5233 (D.C. Cir. Mar. 18, 2025); U.S. Copyright Office, *Copyright Registration Guidance: Works Containing Material Generated by Artificial Intelligence*, 88 Fed. Reg. 16190 (Mar. 16, 2023));

**WHEREAS**, the legal treatment of machine-generated works is not uniform across jurisdictions, and certain jurisdictions may confer, or may in the future confer, some form of protection upon such works;

**WHEREAS**, the Generative Model(s) used to produce the Software were trained by third parties on datasets whose composition, provenance, and licensing status are not known to the Distributor, and the lawfulness of the collection and use of such training data is the subject of pending litigation and unresolved legal questions in multiple jurisdictions;

**WHEREAS**, Generative Models may reproduce, in verbatim or substantially similar form, portions of their training data, which may include material protected by copyright, patent, trade secret, or other rights, or material subject to license terms, including without limitation "copyleft" licenses imposing obligations of attribution or source disclosure;

**NOW, THEREFORE**, the Distributor makes the Software available subject to the following terms and conditions:

---

## ARTICLE 1 — DEFINITIONS

**1.1** "**You**" or "**Recipient**" means any natural person or legal entity that obtains, accesses, uses, copies, modifies, merges, publishes, distributes, sublicenses, sells, or otherwise exploits the Software or any portion thereof.

**1.2** "**Third-Party Rights**" means any and all intellectual property rights, proprietary rights, or contractual rights held by any person other than the Distributor, including without limitation copyrights, moral rights, patents, trademarks, trade secrets, database rights, and rights arising under any open-source, free-software, or proprietary license.

**1.3** "**Training Data**" means any data, code, text, or other material used to train, fine-tune, or otherwise develop any Generative Model used in the creation of the Software.

**1.4** "**Applicable Law**" means all statutes, regulations, judicial decisions, and other legal requirements of any jurisdiction applicable to You or to Your use of the Software.

