## ARTICLE 2 — STATEMENT REGARDING COPYRIGHT STATUS

**2.1 No Assertion of Copyright.** The Distributor makes no claim of copyright ownership in the Software. To the extent the Software consists of material generated by a Generative Model without sufficient human authorship, the Distributor believes, based on the authorities recited above, that such material is not subject to copyright protection under the laws of the United States and is, in effect, in the public domain in that jurisdiction.

**2.2 Fallback Waiver and Dedication.** To the extent that any copyright, neighboring right, *sui generis* database right, or similar right in the Software is or may be held by the Distributor under the laws of any jurisdiction, whether presently or hereafter, the Distributor hereby irrevocably, unconditionally, and perpetually waives, abandons, and surrenders all such rights, and dedicates the Software to the public domain, to the fullest extent permitted by Applicable Law.

**2.3 Fallback License.** Should any waiver or dedication under Section 2.2 be deemed invalid or unenforceable, in whole or in part, the Distributor hereby grants to You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, irrevocable, perpetual license to exercise any and all such rights for any purpose whatsoever, without condition, including commercial purposes.

**2.4 Limitation of Scope.** The foregoing waiver, dedication, and license extend **only** to such rights, if any, as are actually held by the Distributor. **NOTHING HEREIN PURPORTS TO GRANT, AND NOTHING HEREIN SHALL BE CONSTRUED AS GRANTING, ANY LICENSE OR RIGHT UNDER ANY THIRD-PARTY RIGHTS.** The Distributor cannot convey rights it does not possess.

**2.5 No Representation as to Legal Status.** The statements contained in this Article are provided for informational purposes only and do not constitute legal advice. The copyright status of machine-generated works is an evolving area of law, may vary by jurisdiction, and may depend upon the specific degree of human involvement in a given work. The Distributor makes no representation or warranty that any court or authority in any jurisdiction will reach any particular conclusion as to the copyright status of the Software.

